# docs/ Structure Guardrail
Thin structural guardrail only. Conventions and procedure live elsewhere (linked below) — do not restate them here.
## Layout
```
docs/
  DOC_RULES.md         # doc-maintenance procedure + authoritative document roles
  WORKFLOW_BACKLOG.md  # permanently deferred workflow items
  adr/                 # Architecture Decision Records (immutable history)
  prds/                # one PRD per phase (forward intent)
  archive/             # frozen pre-restructure history — closed
```
**Do NOT create new top-level `docs/` directories.** Use the existing ones. If a genuinely new category seems needed, that is a PM decision — surface it, don't invent the directory.
## Where things go
- A per-phase requirements doc → `docs/prds/`. See [prds/README.md](mdc:docs/prds/README.md).
- A recorded architectural decision → `docs/adr/`. See [adr/README.md](mdc:docs/adr/README.md).
- Anything about *how docs are maintained* (write discipline, phase-ship procedure, roles) is governed by [DOC_RULES.md](mdc:docs/DOC_RULES.md) — read it before restructuring docs.
## Archiving
`docs/archive/` is **closed** — it holds frozen pre-restructure history only. Never add to it, never edit it, and never move shipped PRDs into it. Shipped PRDs stay in `docs/prds/` with their status flipped. The archive policy is owned by [DOC_RULES.md](mdc:docs/DOC_RULES.md).
